Skip test_optsize_minsize on riscv64.

The test asserts the loop vectorizer fires, but on targets whose default
CPU exposes no vector registers TargetTransformInfo reports zero vector
registers and LoopVectorize returns before analysis. Affects riscv64,
i686 and s390x; only riscv64 is in the conda-forge matrix.

Upstream: https://github.com/numba/llvmlite/issues/1449

--- a/llvmlite/tests/test_binding.py
+++ b/llvmlite/tests/test_binding.py
@@ -2809,6 +2809,8 @@
         self.assertIn("alloca", orig_asm_optnone)
         self.assertIn("alloca", optimized_asm_optnone)
 
+    @unittest.skipIf(platform.machine().startswith("riscv"),
+                     "riscv64 default CPU exposes no vector registers")
     def test_optsize_minsize(self):
         pb = self.pb(speed_level=3)
 
